,"rel":444},"https:\u002F\u002Fdocs.vatly.com\u002Fopenapi.yaml",[445],"nofollow",",\nbyte-identical to ",[436,448,449],{},"vatly\u002Fvatly-docs\u002Fpublic\u002Fopenapi.yaml"," at\n",[436,452,453],{},"7e71ade32d311b10f79e10c15d0ac03ae32bde97",".\nSHA-256: ",[436,456,457],{},"69640ac82bbba8d101e6aa882facd5f13aa5cf67f38508e5cea18abef03c4940",".\nThe spec's generated-at date is not the retrieval date.\nJS design reference: ",[436,460,461],{},"vatly\u002Fvatly-api-js"," at ",[436,464,465],{},"8b0b920c29f7e7b30bf71b9e379ec0a8a1a22028",".",[433,468,469,470,473],{},"To update, deliberately replace the pinned spec from that production URL, update\nthis provenance, run ",[436,471,472],{},"uv run python scripts\u002Fgenerate.py",", inspect the diff, and\nrun all README checks. CI checks regeneration offline. Do not edit generated files.",[433,475,476,477,480,481,484,485,488,489,492],{},"Output objects preserve extra fields. URLs\u002Femails remain strings. Input enums\nand constraints are generated from the spec. Two observed production differences\nare handled explicitly: empty metadata ",[436,478,479],{},"[]"," normalizes to ",[436,482,483],{},"{}",", and the output\nOneOffProduct.productType is an open string (production returns ",[436,486,487],{},"digital_download",").\nThe checked-in spec is not patched. Response validation failures surface as\n",[436,490,491],{},"VatlyApiError"," with the Pydantic cause; response bodies may contain personal data.\nDo not log them indiscriminately.",[428,494,496],{"id":495},"documentation-sync","Documentation sync",[433,498,499,502,503,506,507,510,511,514,515,518,519,522,523,525,526,528],{},[436,500,501],{},"docs\u002FREADME.md",", ",[436,504,505],{},"API.md",", and the resource guides mirror the JS SDK's layout.\nPushes to ",[436,508,509],{},"main"," affecting ",[436,512,513],{},"docs\u002F**"," notify ",[436,516,517],{},"vatly\u002Fvatly-docs",", which imports\nthese guides automatically. The notifier requires the Actions secret\n",[436,520,521],{},"VATLY_DOCS_DISPATCH_TOKEN"," with Contents: write access to ",[436,524,517],{},".\nKeep relative links portable.\n",[436,527,505],{}," is generated; prose guides are maintained manually.",[428,530,532],{"id":531},"orb-setup","Orb setup",[433,534,535,538],{},[436,536,537],{},".agents\u002Fsetup"," is executable, provisions uv 0.12.9 and Python 3.12, syncs the\nlockfile, and checks imports. It does not read API credentials or make API calls.\nRun twice to check warm behavior. No services or resume repairs are needed.\nIt will become available to project orbs once pushed to the default branch and\nthe repository is connected as an Amp project.",[428,540,542],{"id":541},"pypi-releases","PyPI releases",[433,544,545,553,554,466],{},[441,546,549,552],{"href":547,"rel":548},"https:\u002F\u002Fpypi.org\u002Fproject\u002Fvatly-api-python\u002F0.1.0a2\u002F",[445],[436,550,551],{},"vatly-api-python"," 0.1.0a2","\nwas published on 2026-11-12. The import name remains ",[436,555,556],{},"vatly",[558,559,560,568,584,591],"ol",{},[561,562,563,564,567],"li",{},"Push reviewed code to the public ",[436,565,566],{},"vatly\u002Fvatly-api-python"," repository's main branch.",[561,569,570,571,573,574,576,577,579,580,583],{},"Keep the PyPI trusted publisher for project ",[436,572,551],{},", owner ",[436,575,556],{},",\nrepository ",[436,578,551],{},", workflow ",[436,581,582],{},"release.yml","; leave the environment field blank.\nNo GitHub environment or PyPI token is needed.",[561,585,586,587,590],{},"Update both package-version sources and changelog, run CI, and only with approval\ncreate a new ",[436,588,589],{},"v\u003Cversion>"," tag and publish its GitHub release (mark alphas as prereleases).\nNever reuse a published version or move an existing release tag.",[561,592,593],{},"The release workflow validates\u002Fbuilds first, then exchanges GitHub OIDC for PyPI\ncredentials. Anyone able to publish a matching GitHub release can initiate publication;\nrestrict repository release access accordingly. Publish the SDK before Fluent.",[433,595,596,600],{},[597,598,599],"strong",{},"A private GitHub repository does not make PyPI artifacts private."," Publishing\nuploads the wheel and sdist publicly, including their source and packaged docs.",{"title":602,"searchDepth":603,"depth":603,"links":604},"",2,[605,606,607,608],{"id":430,"depth":603,"text":431},{"id":495,"depth":603,"text":496},{"id":531,"depth":603,"text":532},{"id":541,"depth":603,"text":542},"Vatly Python SDK - Development and release","md",null,{},true,{"title":337,"description":609},"Ra0OdMh1mIpq1hV-hNj0Kq8MFed3IlalYMdX0WeT1sg",[617,619],{"title":50,"path":334,"stem":335,"description":618,"children":-1},"Vatly Python SDK - Webhooks",{"title":300,"path":346,"stem":347,"description":620,"children":-1},"Vatly Python Fluent - Getting started",1794487826369]